{
 "plan": {
  "title": "Scholarship Scheme Progress & Pending Cases",
  "subtitle": "District-wise breakdown of application status and scheme distribution",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Applications",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"scholarship_applicants\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Pending Cases",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\" = 'Pending'",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Disbursed",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\" = 'Disbursed'",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Pending Cases by District",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", COUNT(*) AS pending_count FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\" = 'Pending' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10",
    "x": "district",
    "y": [
     "pending_count"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "kind": "stacked_bar",
    "title": "Scheme Progress by District",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", \"Name of scheme\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1, 2 ORDER BY 1, 2",
    "x": "district",
    "y": [
     "count"
    ],
    "series": "name_of_scheme"
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "kind": "table",
    "title": "Top Districts with Pending Cases",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", COUNT(*) AS total_pending, SUM(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Pending' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS pending, SUM(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Disbursed' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS disbursed FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10"
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "This dashboard tracks the progress of scholarship applications across different districts. Currently, there are {{p1}} total applications in the system, with {{p2}} cases still pending review. \n\nThe bar chart highlights which districts have the highest volume of pending cases, allowing administrators to prioritize resources where they are needed most. \n\nThe stacked bar chart provides a detailed view of how different scholarship schemes are distributed across districts, showing the mix of approved and pending applications for each scheme type. \n\nFinally, the table lists the top districts with the most pending cases, offering a quick reference for follow-up actions."
 },
